From 86a48c6ef9e4b29b6253569fb52bfa6c516a2dba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 04:50:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs: README dates when each model ran here

Qwen3.8-Flash-Next served on the fork from late August 2026; GLM-5.3 Flash served on the Radeon 890M on 2026-10-02 (moe lane cell glm-clamp); upstream v0.6.0 announced both on 2026-10-05.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release documentation for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - documents only; no code path is touched.
---
 README.md | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 6a05704027..704b6fa47b 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -289,10 +289,10 @@ One row per improvement, by the layer it changes. Paths are in this repository.
 **The fork started in July 2026.** Its first commit, which sets up its identity and notices, is dated 22 July 2026.
 Release `b11178-x1i2` carries 828 fork commits on top of upstream `b11178`.
 
-**GLM-5.3 Flash on an integrated GPU, before upstream's release.** We took upstream's GLM-5.3 Flash model code the day
-after it merged (#27773, 30 September) and served the model on the Radeon 890M on 2 October 2026, with its routed
-experts streamed from NVMe. Upstream's v0.6.0 release, which announced GLM-5.3 Flash support, came on 5 October.
-NVMe expert streaming for this model on an integrated GPU is ours; upstream has no such path.
+**When each model ran here.** Qwen3.8-Flash-Next: served on our fork from late August 2026; our MTP drafting with a
+sidecar head followed on 5 October. GLM-5.3 Flash: served on the Radeon 890M on 2 October 2026, routed experts streamed
+from NVMe, built on upstream's model code (#27773). Upstream llama.cpp's v0.6.0 release announced both models on
+5 October 2026. NVMe expert streaming for GLM-5.3 Flash on an integrated GPU is ours.
 
 **Two machines.** Both are mini-PCs with an integrated GPU on one RAM pool.
 
